  "result": "All five tests pass across both test files.\n\nChanges in `netgraph/graph.py`, all built on the existing adjacency-set representation:\n- **`remove_edge(u, v)`** discards the edge from both endpoints' sets, decrements the edge counter, and returns whether an edge was actually removed. Self-loops work because discarding from the same set twice is harmless.\n- **`degree(u)`** returns the size of the node's neighbour set, so a self-loop counts once, matching the spec.\n- **`connected_components()`** runs an iterative depth-first search from each unvisited node in ascending order. Because components are discovered starting from their smallest node, the list is already ordered by smallest member, and each component is sorted before being returned.\n\nAll three methods validate node ids with the same `IndexError` check as the existing API. Nothing under `tests/` was touched.",
